Z||000000||PBJ||12-02-2001||07:37 PM||||I have been reading your "work" or is it "play" on the 4.9's and am wondering about, <P>What distributor I would use with the 93 4.9 pfi using a 730 ecm with the setup you have been describing?<P>Thanks<P>Pete||||reg||1
Z||000001||rockcrawl||12-02-2001||08:23 PM||||You can use any of the Cadillac distributors, 4.1, 4.5, or 4.9. The only difference is that the PFI engines have a cam sensor built in for the sequential injection. The '730 ECM doesn't use the cam sensor. Note that the 4.9 has a shorter oil pump drive shaft because of the redesigned pump, so if the shaft pulls out with the distributor, be carefull to use the correct one. There is also a thrust washer under the distributor gear, if you turn the engine upside down with the distributor out, it will fall out.||||reg||7
Z||000002||jimmybpei||12-02-2001||09:02 PM||||Rockcrawl- Got the caddy running not too bad so far but seems to be running extremmly rich. Would this have any thing to do with the chip you sent me. It almost seems to be running in  a cold start. Is there such as thing as a cold start sensor by the waterneck housing that reads the water temp to adjust the pulse width of the injector once the water temp warms up<P>Thanks for the help.<P>Later<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jimmybpeisig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||12-02-2001||09:12 PM||||The little circuit I sent you was just to get it running without having the Passkey module. That doesn't have anything to do with how well it runs, only wether or not it runs at all. There is a coolant temp sensor in the water neck but I doubt that's the problem. Do you have access to a scanner? Have you tried to pull codes? Do you have the 'check engine' light hooked up? Try to start it with the passkey module disconnected, if it starts without it, you're in limp mode which would explain the fat exhaust.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||12-02-2001||09:20 PM||||Rockcrawl, can I ask a question too?||||reg||1
Z||000005||jimmybpei||12-02-2001||09:55 PM||||rockcrawl- if it does start then it is in limp mode, how do i get it out(diconnect battery or computer)and what if it won't start without the module. Hook it back up and it still runs rich, then it seems as though it stuck in cold idle????<P>Would it then have something to do with the cold start sensor, if indeed ther is one on the caddy motor(not sure)like the v6 has.???<P>The car seems to pull pretty hard, which is good but desperatre hard on gas. I do have a brand new O2 sensor in the car.<P>THanks for the info.<P>Later<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jimmybpeisig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
