Z||000007||rockcrawl||12-02-2001||10:26 PM||||I really don't know a whole lot about the TBI system, can you jumper the ALDL to flash codes? If so, do that first and see what comes up. If it starts without a passkey signal it's in limp mode. When you disconnect power from the ECM it will reset and you'll need the passkey module to get it started again. as soon as it starts and realizes there is a problem, it switches to limp mode again and runs the engine from the fuel backup chips. If it's going into limp mode, it's because you have a sensor failure or other major problem. They do run pretty well in limp mode, just a little rich to keep the engine from burning up until the problem is corrected. I worked with the Caddy PFI ecm for weeks trying to get it to work properly. Limp mode was all I could get. That's when I decided to switch to the F-body ECM. <P>What's up Cooter?||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cooter||12-02-2001||10:56 PM||||OOOOHH OOOOOOOH OOOOOOH! (raises hand and waves to Rockcrawl)<BR>TerryK mentioned that the caddy throttle body (on the 4.9?) uses a different type idle speed control motor. <BR>1.) How did you address this when using the '730 ecm? <BR>2.) With the '730, did you use a 5.0 tuned port prom as a starting point?<P>Thanks a bunch.||||reg||1
